{
 "name": "pen_wall",
 "description": "Polygon pen wall mode: the stroke becomes a strip of quads in the stroke plane, one LEFT / RIGHT vertex pair per stroke point, left = normalize(cross(n_cam, d)) with n_cam the plane normal toward the camera; inner / outer / both rows, mitred interior points without a limit, perpendicular open ends, close reusing the first pair, offset clamped at 0 and offset 0 building nothing, the facing flag not decided (reads 0), and the mirror strip as the reflection of the built wall listed [m(R_i), m(L_i)].",
 "provenance": {
  "schema": 1,
  "source": "live-capture",
  "reference": "ref-editor@11.2v3",
  "method": "gui-gesture",
  "notes": "fresh GUI worker per cell; new empty foreground mesh; wall/offset/close/merge/inset/segments/symmetry set before the first click; real clicks; one readback after the last click",
  "captured_utc": "2026-10-04",
  "harness": "private capture harness",
  "task": "9354"
 },
 "rig": {
  "view": "top orthographic unless a cell says otherwise; 440 px per metre; screen right = +X, screen down = +Z",
  "focus_plane_y": 1.0,
  "click_quantum": "0.005 m at 440 px/m; every clicked point here is on that grid and landed exactly"
 },
 "law": "Wall mode replaces the stroke polygon by a strip of quads in the stroke plane. Rows: for each stroke point i a LEFT vertex L_i and a RIGHT vertex R_i, where left/right are taken relative to the direction of travel AS SEEN FROM THE CAMERA (offset direction for 'left' = normalize(cross(n_cam, d)), n_cam = plane normal pointing at the camera). inner: L = stroke point + offset*left, R = stroke point. outer: L = stroke point, R = stroke point - offset*left. both: L = +offset*left, R = -offset*left (width 2*offset; the stroke point is not a vertex). At an interior point the offset vertex is the MITRE (intersection of the two offset lines, p + w*(n1+n2)/(1+n1.n2), no mitre limit); at an open end it is the perpendicular offset of the end segment. Vertices are emitted per stroke point as [L_i, R_i]; quad i = [L_i, R_i, R_i+1, L_i+1] (2i, 2i+1, 2i+3, 2i+2); close on adds [L_n-1, R_n-1, R_0, L_0] reusing the first pair (independent of merge). Every quad faces the camera; the facing flag is not consulted. Offset is clamped at 0 and offset 0 builds nothing. Symmetry: the mirror strip is the reflection of the original vertices, listed per point as [mirror(R_i), mirror(L_i)] with the same quad template, so it faces the camera too.",
